Card 2 is 1, and the smallest possible card is 1, so the contract settles at exactly 1. An informed buyer will never pay above 1, so only noise traders will buy from me. Their valuation is 1 plus Normal noise with standard deviation 2.8.

I'm long 3 units worth 1 each, so I want to sell at the ask that maximises expected profit per quote. Selling at price p earns x = p − 1 over settlement value, and the buy probability is proportional to 1 − Φ(x/2.8). Maximising x·(1 − Φ(x/2.8)) gives x/2.8 ≈ 0.75, so x ≈ 2.1 and p ≈ 3.1.

